<%- include('../header.ejs'); -%>
<%- include('../nav.ejs'); -%>

<div class="starter-template" style="text-align:left; max-width:900px; margin:0 auto;">
  <h1>Weekly video post</h1>
  <p>What the weekly results video post will contain. Nothing on this page sends anything.</p>

  <% if (!targetsConfigured) { %>
    <p><strong>No Meta credentials are configured on this service, so the post would go nowhere.</strong></p>
  <% } %>

  <h2>Video <small>(<%= aspect %>)</small></h2>
  <%# Same-origin src so this page shows THIS server's file. The absolute URL beneath is
      what Meta fetches — the tables and fixtures previews rendered production's images
      whatever server they ran on, which is the bug that fix exists for. %>
  <video src="<%= videoPath %>" controls preload="metadata"
         style="max-width:360px; width:100%; border:1px solid #ccc; background:#000;"></video>
  <p style="font-size:12px; word-break:break-all; color:#666;">
    Meta fetches <%= videoUrl %>
  </p>
  <p>
    Rendered at 4:5, the same shape as the result cards, so the slides carry no black bars.
    Generated aspects: <%= aspects.join(', ') %>.
    If the player above is empty the video has not been generated yet &mdash; that is a
    404 from <code><%= videoPath %></code>, not a fault in this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Facebook</h2>
  <pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><%= captions.facebook %></pre>

  <h2>Instagram</h2>
  <pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><%= captions.instagram %></pre>
  <p>
    No <code>@</code>-mentions on either, deliberately: a results video names every club
    that played, and mentioning all of them reads as spam rather than courtesy. The weekly
    tables post makes the opposite call because its mentions are the point.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('../footer.ejs') %>

</body>
</html>
